  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzltzpjm3k2c",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I’m still kind of baffled by how surprised or even disbelieving some university admin are when I tell them that many (most? need more data) students are not all in on AI, actually…",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzltzpjm3k2c",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-05T21:51:26.703Z",
      "likes": 274,
      "replies": 7,
      "reposts": 58,
      "score": 7.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 50
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzqkydpmfd2h",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "I think there is too much concern expressed about verification of AI output in everyday work due to a risk of factual errors (there might be things to verify beyond errors, though)\n\nIt used to be true, but data on more recent models suggest they beat human experts in finding facts & checking claims.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzqkydpmfd2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-07T18:52:55.793Z",
      "likes": 66,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzq6762vuc25",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "This can be a golden age of investigative journalism. Analyzing filings, records and public data to go deep into a company or government or whatever used to be something that took a team of journalists a long time, so was relatively rare. Now LLMs can 10x investigative research to help reporting",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzq6762vuc25",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-07T15:04:06.108Z",
      "likes": 73,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 4,
      "score": 6.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 8.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzomjgktvd2h",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Some new data from Anthropic looking at the impact of AI on the sciences by field: \"With current capabilities, if adopted widely, AI could take on 27–52% of the researcher time needed to produce a new study, with a median of 38% across fields...\"\nHere: www.anthropic.com/research/how...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzomjgktvd2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-07T00:15:03.472Z",
      "likes": 67,
      "replies": 14,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 6.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 23.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:6rdthm3ihpqfd7vn2q2ktjrz/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzjsorcdt22y",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "One final remark on all of this. I perceive that people are a bit spooked that the LLM can write neural network weights by hand as opposed to by fitting to data. This is taken as evidence of a special capability. But really, the reason people don’t do this is it’s pointless and stupid.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzjsorcdt22y",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-05T02:22:06.258Z",
      "likes": 65,
      "replies": 4,
      "reposts": 7,
      "score": 5.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 69.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:zlv6yt7cye6eihhy6cl5gl6g/app.bsky.feed.post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "handle": "garymarcus.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Gary Marcus",
      "text": "local-level midterm referendums restricted data center buildout (whether megawatt cap, zoning, outright ban, etc.) at nearly every opportunity.\n\nai oversight a top issue for incoming dem congress..",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/garymarcus.bsky.social/post/3mziv6j7pme2x",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T17:34:02.285Z",
      "likes": 50,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 5.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 0.5,
        "age_hours": 78.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mznjx2btjc25",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Why would people use AI to book uber trips? It’s not hard to use the UI and you get fine control of where the pickup point is. techcrunch.com/2026/11/04/a...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mznjx2btjc25",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-06T13:56:19.394Z",
      "likes": 15,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 33.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:46dh2g4esikgeneoiuzgxftw/app.bsky.feed.post/3mznghdcsxk2k",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "This is just astounding: www.whatisitliketobeafly.com Taking the recently completed neural connectome of a drosophila and making a free playable fly gamebook. \"\n\nVia @mattmuir.bsky.social",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mznghdcsxk2k",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-06T12:53:50.766Z",
      "likes": 12,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 6,
      "score": 5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 35
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I wonder if last night‘s US election results as they relate to AI will finally get through to the folks who have just haven’t been able to accept that not everyone is 100% on board?\n\nI do recognize that a lot of it is specifically data centers which are a narrow slice, but even so!￼",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzisiq3hnc2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-04T16:46:03.917Z",
      "likes": 28,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 4.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 0.5,
        "age_hours": 79.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzjfistyyc2a",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I do think that is part of it but I also think that some of it is just the very personal impact thing - like some people might not actually care much about AI but they don’t want a noisy annoying thing in their backyard.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3mzjfistyyc2a",
